¶Enas antras exaphanizetai aphenontas piso tou ena mpaoulo gemato keimena. To polutimo auto periekhomeno katalegei sta kheria enos paliou tou philou, o opoios stadiaka anakaluptei oti oi istories pou aphegountai ta keimena kruboun ena idiaitero menuma gi' auton.
Pos sundeetai enas khamaileon me to khorio pou onomazetai Anamones; Poso duskole einai e apodrase apo kathe khorio; Poia einai e euthune ton <>sten exaphanise tou antra; Pos antimetopizeis tous diephtharmenous politikous, tous periergous demosiographous, tous sunaisthematikous ependutes kai tous sumpherontologous polites; Pos diakheirizesai ten apoleia tou patera sou;
Mia istoria enelikioses kai epodunes anazeteses tautotetas.
To politiko, to prosopiko kai anatreptiko khroniko tes epimones apopeiras enos neou antra na ginei o eautos tou.
Stelekhos etaireias, demosiographos, suggrapheas, agrotes e aplos enas akome muthomanes; Poios einai telika o Giorgos Moskhonas;"Ø
¨To 1899, o megalos poietes Rainer Maria Rilke - eikosiduakhronos tote - ekane ena megalo taxidi ste Rosia. Gnorise ton terastio Tolstoi, gnorise aplous khorikous kai georgous, agapese ta aperanta topia.
Molis xanagurise sto Monakho, egrapse mesa se ephta nukhtes autes tis uperokhes istories, tis bathia stokhastikes kai poietikes, ki ostoso gemates drosia kai upogeio khioumor.
O Kalos Theoules tou Rilke paskhizei na katalabei tous anthropous - ten ora pou oi anthropoi paskhizoun na sullaboun ten idea tou Theou.
Paskhizei na ginei kathemerinos - ten ora pou oi anthropoi anazetoun to Uperbatiko. Kai, to spoudaiotero: autos o Kalos Theoules den ekhei kamia threskeutike tautoteta."∂
≥It's a match made in rock & roll heaven when two of the greatest bands get together to make sweet music.
Join The Archies & Josie and the Pussycats on a whirlwind tour full of rockin' rivalries, romance, and revenge!
What starts with a kiss turns in to an all-out love smackdown when Archie falls for Valerie!
But when Betty & Veronica find out, it could be the end of not only their romance, but of The Archies and The Pussycats, too!"∏
µE Ispanida metaphrastria tou Patrik Le Phermor Ntolores Pagias episkephtheke prote phora ton suggraphea sto spiti tou sten Kardamule to 2009. E prote aute sunantese etan e aparkhe mias philias pou diateretheke mekhri to telos tes zoes tou suggraphea. Mesa apo to khrono pou perasan mazi kai tis suzeteseis tous gennetheke auto to biblio. Ena anthropino skiagraphema tou Agglou suggraphea kai tolmerou taxideute, tou goeteutikou kai gennaiodorou Panti, pou ezese ta teleutaia khronia tes zoes tou peritrigurismenos apo philous, pota kai, pano ap' ola, ta biblia tou."º
πThis book provides an up-to-date, in-depth treatment of the major issues, theories and findings in perception and representation. It introduces a cross-section of different research methods and the reader is encouraged, by means of activities and self-assessment questions, to become an active participant in cognitive psychology. In particular, the student is introduced to conceptual categorisation, object recognition and face recognition by working through actual problems and so is able to test and develop theoretical frameworks by 'hands-on' experience. The first edition of this book established itself as an accessible, contemporary introduction to this area. This second edition has been extensively rewritten to take account of the latest research, including developments in neuropsychology and computer modelling."º
πTo proi tes 28es Iouniou tou 1914, otan o Arkhidoukas Pherdinandos, diadokhos tes Austrias, ephtase me te suzugo tou ston siderodromiko stathmo tou Saragebou, e Europe zouse akome en eirene. Triantaepta meres argotera briskotan se polemo. E sugkrouse pou akolouthese aphese pano apo dekapente ekatommuria nekrous, katestrepse treis autokratories kai allaxe rizika ten pagkosmia istoria.
Pos mporesan ta Balkania -mia periphereia apomakrusmene apo ta europaika kentra tes iskhuos kai tou ploutou- na ginoun to epikentro enos dramatos tetoiou megethous; O Kristopher Klark apopheugei ton peirasmo na apodosei ten euthune tes anaphlexes se mia apokleistike aitia e mia monadike khora. Anikhneuei tous dromous pou odegesan ston polemo pernontas ap' ola ta krisima kentra apophaseon ste Bienne, to Berolino, ten Petroupole, to Parisi, to Londino, to Beligradi, kai parakolouthontas lepto pros lepto tis kataigistikes exelixeis. Apokaluptei etsi enan thrummatismeno kosmo astatheias kai eridas, mia Europe epibarumene malista me mia moiraia ki atelesphore omada politikon arkhegon. Autoi oi kubernontes, pou kamaronan gia to neoterismo kai ton orthologismo tous, tsalaboutousan apo krise se krise ospou epeisan ton eauto tous oti o polemos etan e mone apantese.
Biblio aristotekhnika grammeno kai diexodika tekmeriomeno se nees ereunes, Oi upnobates einai o entuposiakos apologismos tes purodoteses kai tes ekrexes enos apo ta megalutera sumbanta tes sugkhrones istorias."≈
¬Erotas dunatos den uparkhei para mono sto teleio suntairiasma ton duo suntrophon... Kai kathos den uparkhoun duo atoma apolutos omoia, kathe andras prepei na brei se mian orismene gunaika tis idiotetes pou antapokrinontai kalutera stis dikes tou idiotetes, pantote apo ten optike gonia ton paidion pou prokeitai na gennethoun. Oso pio spanio einai auto to idaniko tairiasma, toso pio spanios einai kai o pragmatika megalos erotas.
Arthur Schopenhauer"Œ
À<>.
<>.
E istoria aphora ten idiomorphe sumbiose duo gunaikon, pou den tis khorizei monon e sumbatike metrese tou khronou, delade mia apostase epta aionon, alla kai khilies duo alles sunthekes (sumbatikes e ousiastikes), kai mesa apo auten xetuligontai ta ulika tes tekhnes tes gnostes suggraphea se mia <>ulikon pou onomazetai <>."ÿ
’To biblio analuei kai ermeneuei tis ekplektikes allages pou prokalesan e politike Gallike Epanastase kai e agglike Biomekhanike Epanastase: ta "palaia kathestota" katarreoun mprosta ste duname ton neon kapitalistikon khoron. E istoria tes dittes epanastases, ostoso, den einai aplos e istoria tou thriambou tes neas astikes koinonias einai kai e istoria tes emphanises ton dunameon pou, mesa s' enan aiona apo to 1848, emelle na metatrepsoun ten epektase se surriknose."ÿ
’Ouasigkton, 21 Oktobriou 1967. Mia thalassa diadeloton, pou alloi upologizoun se 20.000 kai alloi se 200.000 (analoga me ten ephemerida pou diabazoun), axionoun ton termatismo tou polemou sto Bietnam, eno sta skalia tou Pentagonou tous perimenoun me agries diatheseis omospondiakoi astunomkoi kai enoploi stratiotes. Anamesa stous diadelotes kai enas suggrapheas, pou onomazetai Norman Meeler. E idiomorphe summetokhe tou ste diadelose kathos kai oi dioratikes tou episemanseis tha gennesoun ena klasiko ergo pou erkhetai na anatrepsei te logike tou paradosiakou reportaz.
Dianooumenoi kai khipis, astunomikoi kai klerikoi, poietes kai stratonomoi ginontai sta kheria tou Meieler oi eroes enos bibliou pou perigraphei ta gegonota me ten tekhnike tou muthistorematos, gia na apodosei kalutera ten aletheia.
To aphegema auto pou antimetopizei <>brabeuteke me ta duo megalutera brabeia ton EPA: to Brabeio Poulitzer kai to Ethniko Brabeio Bibliou.
"Me mpalzakike orme o Meiler perigraphei tous omiletes, to plethos kai ten exarse tou, tous astunomikous, ton periguro. Kai me to biblio tou auto demiourgei ena neo logotekhniko eidos, prodromos tou opoiou uperxe ligo noritera me to En psukhro o Trouman Kapote: te Nea Demosiographia. Antistrephontas ton orismo tou Mpalzak oti "to muthistorema einai e idiotike istoria ton ethnon", o Meiler phortizei ton demosio logo kai ta gegonota, emprotheta kai peismatika, me ten exarse kai to drama tes atomikes suneideses. Oi straties tes nukhtas paramenoun biblio-stathmos toso gia to diko tou ergo oso kai gia to sunolo tes metapolemikes amerikanikes pezographias. Den uparkhei amphibolia oti diabazontas to o europaios anagnostes ekhei mias protes taxeos eukairia na katalabei ti einai kai ti semainei e sugkhrone Amerike: ta dilemmata pou thetei ston eauto tes kai tis prokleseis pou apeuthunei sten upoloipe Duse kai ston kosmo. Kai monon to teleutaio kephalaio tou bibliou einai san na milaei gia tis EPA tou semera..."
(ANASTASES BISTONITES, To Bema, 25/5/2003)"Ÿ
÷19 Apriliou 1936. Mesanukhta skhedon, tha gennetho akribos se ena lepto, tha ertho ston kosmo stis 20 Apriliou. Anemera ton genethlion tou Phurer mas. Tha eimai etsi eulogemenos apo tous germanikous theous kai tha anagnorisoun sto prosopo mou ton prototoko tes anoteres phules. Tes arias phules. Autes pou sto exes tha kuriarkhesei ston upoloipo kosmo. Eimai to paidi tou mellontos. Ekho sullephthei khoris agape. Khoris Theo. Khoris nomo. Khoris tipote allo para duname kai orge. Tha dagkono anti na pipilao, tha ourliazo anti na klapsourizo. Tha miso anti na agapo. Khail Khitler!
O Max einai to teleio prototupo tou programmatos <>, to opoio ethese se epharmoge o Khimler. Gunaikes epilegmenes apo tous nazi phernoun ston kosmo katharous ekprosopous tes arias phules, mia idanike nea genia pou proorizetai na anagennesei te Germania kai meta ole ten katekhomene apo to Raikh Europe.
Ena biblio-stathmos, exairetika tekmeriomeno, pou milaei me diaphoretiko tropo gia ton nazismo.
Ena sugklonistiko anagnosma, apo to opoio den mporei kaneis na bgei alobetos. (Apo ten parousiase sto opisthophullo tou bibliou)"‹
Ÿ"To antikeimeniko kai to apoluto pneuma" apoteloun to deutero kai to trito antistoikha tmema tes "Philosophias tou pneumatos" tou Khegkel. Ste "Philosophia tou antikeimenikou pneumatos" o philosophos pragmateuetai te dialektike par-ousia tou pneumatos mesa ston kosmo. Prokeitai st' aletheia gia to pneuma tou kosmou, pou enuparkhei mesa sten istoria kai ten koinonia tou anthropou. Enuparkhei delade os to "Apoluto" sten empragmate suntheke tou: ston autoprosdiorismo tou mesa stous koinonikous kai politikous thesmous, sto politeuma, sto kratos kai sten istoria ton kraton. Ste "Philosophia tou apolutou pneumatos" sunaphos o Khegkel parakolouthei ton apoluta energo auto-prosdiorismo tou pneumatos, os ennoiologikou Olou, sto epipedo tes tekhnes, tes threskeias kai tes philosophias. Auto to Olo apobainei telika ste glossa tou anthropou: noeseos noesis."Á
‰"Se mia epokhe duskolion, e kathemerine zoe ginetai askese sten epibiose. Oi anthropoi zoun mono to semera. Spania koitazoun piso, gia na me paradothoun se mia paralutike nostalgia kai an koitazoun mpros, einai gia na doun pos mporoun na prostateuthoun apo tis sumphores pou skhedon oloi perimenoume semera. E sunaisthematike isorropia apaitei semera enan elakhisto eauto, kai okhi ton epibletiko eauto tou prosphatou parelthontos".
Etsi xekina to biblio tou o Kristopher Las kai stis triakosies selides pou akolouthoun sterizei ta legomena tou. (Apo ten parousiase sto opisthophullo tou bibliou)
O Kristopher Las sto biblio auto askholeitai me ten epidrase tes sugkhrones koinonias ste diamorphose tou Eautou. O 20os aionas ephere ten ektene biomekhanopoiese, te bia se ektase kai morphe protophaneis sten Istoria, ton uperplethusmo, ton oikologiko kinduno kai ten auxese tou ogkou kai takhutetas metadoses tes plerophorias. Tautokhrona, ephere kai mia aneu proegoumenou koinonike kai politike poluplokoteta. E aisthese tes klimakas tou koinonikou perigurou pou periballei ton kathe anthropo megalose kata polu, eno o auxemenos ruthmos ton exelixeon ton anagkase na metatrapei apo eremo diamorphote tes pragmatikotetas tou se dromea pou prospathei na prolabei tis exelixeis. To me-oikeio, takheos exelissomeno kai apeiletiko auto periballon emphanizetai uperbolika "megalo" kai ekhthriko pros ten eggene tase tou anthropou na epiblethei ston periguro tou. Apotelesma: e surriknose tou Eautou sta apolutos basika stoikheia tou, o periorismos tou se mia katastase diarkous polemikes etoimotetas. Kai opos se kathe polemo, e epibiose metatrepetai se proteuousa proteraioteta, toso polu malista pou kathistatai autoskopos, parablepontas ten anagke anazeteses opoioudepote allou noematos peran tes idias tes epibioses. E ugies uparxiake skhese tou anthropou me to periballon tou diarregnuetai kathos autos metatrepetai se polemiste: anasphales, epithetikos kai kairoskopos, etoimos na kanei to katheti pou pisteuei oti tha katasigasei ten anasphaleia tou, xekhna poso bathia sundedemene einai e moira tou me te moira ton allon anthropon kai tou euruterou periballontos tou. Ta parapano apoteloun mikro mono meros tou noematos tou bibliou, noematos pou uposterizetai apo mia embrithe epikheirematologia e opoia einai ektenestate se klimaka kai se periekhomeno: gia na uposterixei ta legomena tou, o Las mas taxideuei se plethos noetikon topothesion, opos stis nazistikes sugkentroseis tes Germanias tou 1938 e tis allelepidraseis ton phroudikon diastromatoseon tes psukhes. Ena biblio okhi eukolo, pou omos, opos katheti duskolo, antameibei ten prospatheia me enan anektimeto plouto gnoses pou xeperna kata polu ta oria ta opoia tukhon thetei o titlos. (Marios Damoulianos, per. Strange, 2008)"Í
ÁLittle-known Graeme Obree became international cycling's most unlikely star, capturing the public's imagination with his innovative engineering and design skills and unique training regiments. When he broke world records and won championships, the cycling authorities outlawed both his bike and his tucked riding position. He invented the ""Superman"" riding style and triumphed again. But while battling authorities and other cyclists, Obree was also battling a much more serious threat: bipolar disorder. In ""The Flying Scotsman, Obree tells his remarkable story with brutal honesty and unexpected humor. Beginning with his troubled childhood in Ayrshire, where the bike was his only escape, Obree recounts his turbulent life and career, describing what drove him to not only break records, but to attempt suicide on three separate occasions. Long known for his courage on the track, here Obree demonstrates a different kind of courage as he movingly lays bare his struggle with manic depression."Ò
ÓStis meres mas, e uparxe tou kratous theoreitai autonoete. Diamarturomaste gia tis apaiteseis tou. Paraponoumaste oti pareisphreei oloena kai perissotero se upotheseis pou palaiotera theorountan idiotikes. Mas einai, omos, skhedon adunato na phantastoume te zoe khoris auto. Ston semerino kosmo, e kheirotere moira pou mporei na lakhei s' enan anthropo einai na men ekhei kratos.
Oi palies morphes koinonikes anagnorises ekhoun semera papsei na einai apoluta anagkaies. Enas anthropos mporei na zesei mia ligo-polu olokleromene zoe dikhos oikogeneia, dikhos monimo topo katoikias, dikhos threskeutike entaxe* alla an den ekhei kratos, einai ena tipota. Den ekhei dikaiomata, den ekhei asphaleia, ki oi eukairies tou gia mia demiourgike prosopike poreia tha einai medamines. Den uparkhei epi tes ges soteria exo apo to plaisio enos organomenou kratous.
Aphou den mporoume na xephugoume ap' to kratos, ekhei semasia na to katanoesoume. Enas tropos na to petukhoume auto, einai na meletesoume ten istoria tou - na exetasoume pos kai pote anadutheke e sugkekrimene morphe organoses, ti eidous anagkes kalupte, se poies arkhes etan basismene. Mia melete ton katabolon tou neoterou europaikou kratous tha mporouse endekhomenos na photisei kapos ta gnorismata kai ta problemata tou kratous ton emeron mas. Mporei na mas boethesei na entopisoume tis diaphores anamesa stous poikilous tupous kratous kai na exegesoume gia poio logo orismena krate diathetoun perissotero euruthmes kai apotelesmatikes morphes organoses apo alla."Û
Mia plousia kleronomos e Linet Ritzgouaie kataphernei na proselkuei ta blemmata, alla kai to misos oson briskontai guro tes. Mesa s' autous pou tha ethelan to kako tes sugkatalegetai kai e kalutere phile tes, e Zakelin nte Mpelphor, xepesmene aristokratissa. Ekhei kathe logo malista, kathos e Linet molis prosphata pantreuteke ton diko tes agapemeno. E Zakelin akolouthei tous neonumphous kai stoikheionei kathe stigme tous.
To zeugari thelontas na apallagei ap' ten okhlere parousia tes katapheugei sto polutelestato atmoploio Karnak, pou katapleei sta esukha nera tou Neilou. Dustukhos sto ploio epibainei ki enas stugeros dolophonos pou <>guro tou ptomata alla kai o Erakles Pouaro pou antimetopizei ten pio <>kai skoteine upothese tes karieras tou"¯
ıTi akribos einai mia <>; To idio anarotietai ki o aphegetes autou tou ekplektikou, mikrou kai sumpuknomenou muthistorematos pou, aphou to katapieis, ekregnutai mesa sou se sophes iamatikes doseis kalaisthesias, melagkholias kai sugkineses.
Gi' alle mia phora, o Patrick Modiano, autos o eupatrides tes nostalgias, kataduetai sto skoteino pegadi tou khronou, mepos kai spasei to rekor paramones kato ap' to semera - me te diaphora, oti, kai pali, autos pou krataei ten anapnoe tou, einai o anagnostes...
Gi' alle mia phora, sto gnorimo kai gnorima sunarpastiko sumpan tou Modiano, parelthon, paron kai mellon dialuontai (e sugkheontai;), kathos mia xekourdiste mneme paskhizei na anasuntethei, anazetontas to noema tes zoes, alla kai to noema
tes anazeteses."˘
ˆE pagomene eremia tou makrinou Borra enepneuse ston Tzak Lonton to Kalesma tis agrias phuses, tis romalees tou istories epikindunon peripeteion, opou kuriarkhei to enstikto tes epibioses. Me gregore kai glaphure aphegese, oi istories pou perilambanontai edo pragmateuontai to kurio thema tou Tzak Lonton - to nomo tou ropalou kai tou skulodontou, ten enstiktode epistrophe tou anthropou sten protogone sumperiphora otan brisketai antimetopos me tis agries dunameis tes phuses.
Epaxia loipon to "Kalesma tes agrias phuses" kharise diethne anagnorise ston Tzak Lonton kai theoreitai ena apo ta klasika aristourgemata tou 20ou aiona."˝
˙BONUS: This edition contains an excerpt from Dean Koontz's The City.
With his bestselling blend of nail-biting intensity, daring artistry, and storytelling magic, Dean Koontz returns with an emotional roller coaster of a tale filled with enough twists, turns, shocks, and surprises for ten ordinary novels. Here is the story of five days in the life of an ordinary man born to an extraordinary legacy--a story that will challenge the way you look at good and evil, life and death, and everything in between.
Jimmy Tock comes into the world on the very night his grandfather leaves it. As a violent storm rages outside the hospital, Rudy Tock spends long hours walking the corridors between the expectant fathers' waiting room and his dying father's bedside. It's a strange vigil made all the stranger when, at the very height of the storm's fury, Josef Tock suddenly sits up in bed and speaks coherently for the frist and last time since his stroke.
What he says before he dies is that there will be five dark days in the life of his grandson--five dates whose terrible events Jimmy will have to prepare himself to face. The first is to occur in his twentieth year; the second in his twent-third year; the third in his twenty-eighth; the fourth in his twenty-ninth; the fifth in his thirtieth.
Rudy is all too ready to discount his father's last words as a dying man's delusional rambling. But then he discovers that Josef also predicted the time of his grandson's birth to the minute, as well as his exactheight and weight, and the fact that Jimmy would be born with syndactyly--the unexplained anomal of fused digits--on his left foot. Suddenly the old man's predictions take on a chilling significance.
What terrifying events await Jimmy on these five dark days? What nightmares will he face? What challenges must he survive? As the novel unfolds, picking up Jimmy's story at each of these crisis points, the path he must follow will defy every expectation. And with each crisis he faces, he will move closer to a fate he could never have imagined. For who Jimmy Tock is and what he must accomplish on the five days when his world turns is a mystery as dangerous as it is wondrous--a struggle against an evil so dark and pervasive, only the most extraordinary of human spirits can shine through."˛
˚"Koita, mama, astrapes!" ourliaxe e Monika blepontas ta elektrika plokamia na kapsalizoun ourano kai thalassa. To phorema kollese monomias epano tes ki arkhise na tremei. Ma giati erthan edo; Mepos e metera skopeuei na autoktonesei; Mepos den antexe auto pou sunebe me ton Uparkho kai thelei na pnigei gia na parei ekdikese; E Stella, omos, pou e kataigida ten enthousiaze, xepatone ede me tis oples tes ta sanidia tou katastromatos. O, einai bebaio pos skopeuei na rikhtei sten pisina, prolabe na skephtei e Monika, ki amesos e metera ten arpaxe ki arkhise na trekhei, astraphtontas ki e idia san ton ourano, to idio tromere me te thuella, isaxies ki isodunames e metera ki e thuella, to gelio tes ki o keraunos, etrekhan trabontas te Monika exo ap' ta oria. Mama, phobamai! tolmese na skephtei ki amesos "khrap!", to stoma ton neron ten katapie.
Otan, mia aionioteta argotera, anebeke sten epiphaneia, antikrise to eutukhismeno soma tes meteras anaskela, na khamogela stis ripes pou to mastigonan. Koitaxe kalutera. Uparkhoun phores pou e metera den einai e metera, alla mia arkhaia theoteta, pou t' aplomena mpratsa tes ginontai phtera kai ta xediplonei agerokhe, san phlampoura tou Agiou Markou, san semaies tou ELAS, san "almpatros" tou Mpontlair. Kai anupsonetai. Kai 'su, pou phobosoun pos tha katakremnistei sto erebos, to blepeis auto kai thamponesai.
To "Kalo aima, kako aima" einai mia sulloge diegematon opou to pragmatiko kai to phantastiko, to tragiko kai to komiko, to sosto kai to lathos, to kalo kai to kako, anameignuontai kai periplekontai, me apotelesma o anagnostes na odegeitai se enan kosmo skhedon muthiko. Oi eroes ton istorion den einai sunethismenoi anthropoi, alla uparxeis poietikes, oi opoies antistekontai sten exomoiose kai ton aphanismo mesa apo praxeis uperbases pou, eno ston "pragmatiko kosmo" tha emenan sten aphaneia, mesa apo ten idiaitere graphe tes Eleonoras Stathopoulou anadeiknuoun ton krupho eroismo tous.
Ola ta prosopa ton diegematon ekphrazoun mia lakhtara gia lutrose. Tha katapheroun telika na te zesoun; Den tha to mathoume pote me sigouria, akome ki an mia gramme prin apo to telos oles oi kampanes khtupoun anastasima."␀␀ê@"	)\è¬ı(@"	)\è¬ı(@"	H·zÆG@"	H·zÆG@"	H·zÆG@"	ffffff
